# What each node runs when a start request gives it work — the source both
# fleet files point at. The image bakes a copy beside the gateway's fleet
# files, so the gateway's own wakes resolve it from inside the container.
#
# The BASEURL is the point: it binds the engine to every interface. Without
# it llama-server binds 127.0.0.1, the daemon reports the engine loopback-only,
# and the gateway — a different container — is right to refuse routing to it.
# The client's Spinloop has no BASEURL at all: it names no engine, because it
# never talks to one.
PROVIDER llamacpp
MODEL    org/fake-model
ALIAS    fake-model
CONTEXT  4096
BASEURL  http://0.0.0.0:8080/v1
